data.content:
The discount is implemented and all 11 tests in the integration project pass: the 9 approved scenario rows and the 2 architecture tests. The build has no warnings. The unit-test project has no tests, so the run covered only the integration project.

- **`LoyaltyDiscount.CentsFor`** (new, in the Domain project) applies the four approved rules:
  - tier rate: Bronze 5, Silver 7, Gold 9 points;
  - order-size bonus: +1 point at 50.00 and above, +3 at 200.00 and above;
  - the 10-point ceiling;
  - the discount taken on the original subtotal and rounded down to the cent.
- **`CalculatePayableTotal.For`** now returns the subtotal minus that discount.

I added nothing beyond the approved rules. I did not check the 100% coverage gate mentioned in `Directory.Build.props`.
